@title 911 Call Path and Failover
@subtitle Marrow County Emergency Communications District
@author Public Safety Systems
@date 2026-09-30
@width wide

# Overview
Calls arrive from the telephone carriers into the Primary Dispatch Center, where they are routed to the computer-aided dispatch (CAD) system. A Backup Dispatch Center across the county can take over if the primary is lost.

!!! The Backup Dispatch Center is activated only when the shift supervisor declares the primary unavailable. It never takes over automatically.

# Call path
diagram calls dir=LR title="911 call path"
calls: callers "Callers" user
calls: carriers "Telecom Carriers" ext
calls: router "Call Router" svc focus
calls: cada "CAD Server A" svc "active" focus
calls: cadb "CAD Server B" svc "hot standby"
calls: radio "Radio Gateway" svc
calls: standby "Standby Call Router" svc
calls: replica "CAD Replica" db
calls: gis "State GIS Service" ext
calls: units "Field Units" team
calls: callers -> carriers : voice and caller location
calls: carriers -> router : SIP trunks
calls: router -> cada : call record
calls: cada -> cadb : state sync
calls: cada --> replica : async replication
calls: router --> standby : heartbeat
calls: cada -> gis : address lookup
calls: cada -> radio : dispatch message
calls: radio -> units : P25 radio
calls: group primary "Primary Dispatch Center" router, cada, cadb, radio
calls: group backup "Backup Dispatch Center" standby, replica
calls: legend

# Failover targets
kpi Call routing | 30 s | to Standby Call Router
kpi CAD | 2 min | CAD Server B takes over
kpi Replica lag | < 5 s | CAD Replica
kpi Backup center | 10 min | staffed and taking calls

table = component,takes over,target; Call routing,Standby Call Router,within 30 seconds; CAD,CAD Server B,within 2 minutes; CAD data,CAD Replica,lags by under 5 seconds; Whole dispatch center,Backup Dispatch Center,fully staffed and taking calls within 10 minutes

!! The 10-minute backup-center clock starts only once the shift supervisor declares the primary unavailable. Nothing fails over to the backup center automatically.
